// The poseik package: inverse kinematics, foot placement, look-at, hand
// reach and grip, and pose blending with a small animation state machine,
// for the skeletons and poses of the bonepose package (and beside walkgait,
// whose walk it can correct on uneven ground). A program reaches it with
// 'import poseik'.
//
// Every solver changes a 'Pose' (bonepose's: one local transform per bone)
// and keeps the bones' model-space transforms ('models') current, so solvers
// chain: walk, then plant the feet, then look, then reach. All of it is
// plain data in and out: no solver keeps a reference to a skeleton, and
// the only state is what is named (a FootPlacer's smoothed pelvis, an
// Animator's clock and fade).
//
// - limb.cone      two-bone analytic IK with a pole vector and an interior
//                  angle range (a knee that cannot hyperextend), the law of
//                  cosines as bonepose's solveTwoBone has it, applied to a
//                  skeleton's three bones
// - chain.cone     chains of any length: FABRIK (Aristidou and Lasenby,
//                  "FABRIK: a fast, iterative solver for the inverse
//                  kinematics problem", Graphical Models 2011) and CCD (Wang
//                  and Chen, "A combined optimization method for solving the
//                  inverse kinematics problem of mechanical manipulators",
//                  1991), both with a per-joint cone or hinge constraint
// - foot.cone      FootPlacer: lift and plant each foot on ground given by a
//                  height query, lower or raise the pelvis, tilt the soles
//                  to the ground normal
// - lookat.cone    the head turned to a point, the neck and spine sharing
//                  the turn, clamped to what a body can do
// - reach.cone     a hand to a position and an orientation (a grip), the
//                  arm bent by the limb solver
// - blend.cone     linear, masked and additive blends of poses; keyframed
//                  Clips; a 1-D BlendSpace (idle, walk, run by speed)
// - animator.cone  an Animator: states that play a clip or a blend space,
//                  transitions with conditions on named parameters, and timed
//                  cross-fades
//
// Conventions are bonepose's: right-handed, y up, metres, f32; a being faces
// -z at rest; a positive yaw turns it left. A 'world' transform is the
// model's placement in the world (a position and a rotation about y); a ground
// query is a closure from world (x, z) to the ground's height, the same
// 'ground' that walkgait takes.

mod poseik;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import bonepose use *;
